    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds a `selfLink` field to owner responses, returning `/api/owners/{id}`.\n\nSince the test reads the field back via `GET /api/owners/{id}` and `OwnerDto` is generated from the OpenAPI spec, I made two changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `selfLink` string property to the `Owner` schema, so `OwnerDto` gets the field generated onto it.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct mapping that derives it from the entity id:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"selfLink\", expression = \"java(owner.getId() == null ? null : \\\"/api/owners/\\\" + owner.getId())\")\n   ```\n\nThis flows through both `RespondWithOwner` (GET) and `RespondWithOwnerCreated` (POST) since both map via `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`. `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsSelfLink` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures).",
